//@version=6
// BTC ATTACK 52 - RSI/PRICE BULLISH DIVERGENCE, TARGET LOOKBACK SCALED 2x FURTHER OUT.
//
// THE STORED PROMPT still asks for Attack 37's filter stack (a sixth time). THE DOCS OVERRIDE IT:
// Attack 41 closed Attack 37 as a development target, Attack 43 closed the sweep-reversal FAMILY,
// Attack 47 died on the ~77% sample wall on the current champion (Attack 46), and Attack 51's own
// QUEUE item 2 is the specific, named next step this cycle executes -- not a fresh "propose a new
// mechanism" fallback, a queued, narrower variant of an already-built one.
//
// ==================== WHAT THIS IS ====================
// IDENTICAL mechanism to Attack 51 (RSI(14)/price bullish divergence at a confirmed swing low,
// ta.pivotlow(5,5), non-repainting). ONE change: the target lookback (`tgtLook`) is doubled, 20 -> 40,
// per Attack 51's own queue item 2 ("target lookback at 2x or 3x the pivot lookback... a narrower,
// testable variant for a future cycle"). Nothing else moves -- not leftBars/rightBars, not rsiLen, not
// the R floor, not maxBars. This is a single-term change on an already-falsified base, evaluated fresh
// against the kill rule, not folded into the RATCHET (Attack 51 was discarded outright, there is
// nothing of it left to ratchet against).
//
// CLAIM, UNCHANGED FROM ATTACK 51: when price prints a LOWER confirmed swing low but RSI(14) prints a
// HIGHER reading at that same swing, the new low lacks momentum confirmation and tends to resolve back
// toward the recent range. Attack 51 falsified this at 0.72680011 PF (223 trades) with a diagnosed
// cause: the target (prior 20-bar high) shared its short lookback with the pivot search (5/5), so the
// level aimed at was not reliably far enough above the entry to outweigh a stop planted at a low that,
// by definition, had just been freshly broken. THIS BUILD tests whether doubling the target search
// window to 40 bars (roughly 2x the pivot-to-pivot span the divergence is measured over) finds a
// genuinely more distant resistance level, without touching the entry/stop geometry that Attack 51 did
// not diagnose as the problem.
//
// ==================== MECHANICS, NO ARRAYS, NO UDFs ====================
// Same as Attack 51: ta.pivotlow(low, leftBars, rightBars), non-repainting, confirmed rightBars after
// the actual low. Two `var float` pairs (not arrays) hold the two most recent confirmed pivot lows and
// the RSI reading at each, both read from the identical historical bar via a [rightBars] shift.
//
// AUDIT, one line per leg:
//   R >= 0.8% (LESSON 3) - enforced by EXCLUSION via rBig, unchanged from Attack 51. A divergence whose
//        stop is too close to clear the floor is SKIPPED, never widened.
//   Stop beyond STRUCTURE (LESSON 5) - slPx = lastPivLow, the confirmed pivot-low PRICE. Unchanged.
//   Each leg separately (LESSON 6) - LONG ONLY, unchanged. The bearish mirror remains an outstanding,
//        separately-built leg, not assumed here.
//   BINDING (E17) - divNow still requires TWO independently confirmed pivots in a specific relative
//        order; doubling tgtLook does not loosen this, so the trade count is expected to land close to
//        Attack 51's 223 on H1, not to inflate. Read the count before quoting any ratio (LESSON 12).
//   REDUNDANCY (E14) - rBig constrains STOP distance (an absolute % floor); rrOk only checks the target
//        sits above entry (existence, not a size threshold) -- unchanged, still non-overlapping.
//   LATCH IN SEQUENCE (LESSON 8) - unchanged: pivot and its RSI both come from an already-confirmed,
//        historical bar; the entry trigger uses only already-known past data.
//   TARGET IS A LEVEL, NOT A MULTIPLE (HARD LESSON 41/47) - tpPx = res, now the prior 40-bar high
//        instead of the prior 20-bar high. Still a level, never an rr multiple; rr is measured, not set.
//   SL and TP FIXED AT ENTRY. No trailing, no averaging down, no martingale.
//
// OUTCOMES REGISTERED BEFORE THE RUN (LESSON 17):
//   * PRE-2024 HALF (H1, never-tuned) BELOW 1.0 -> KILL RULE. Discard, do not run H2, do not filter
//        further (do not also try 3x -- that is a second, separate future-cycle test per the queue,
//        not a rescue of this one).
//   * H1 CLEARS 1.0 BUT UNDER ~30 TRADES -> a DIRECTION, not a result (LESSON 12); report as such and
//        still run H2 since credits allow it, but neither half is quotable as a ratio.
//   * BOTH HALVES CLEAR 1.0 WITH A DEFENSIBLE COUNT (>=30 EACH) -> the reachable-target fix worked;
//        this becomes a second genuinely-new, both-halves-positive family alongside the sweep-reversal
//        family (Attack 37) and queues for its own filter-stack treatment.
//   * TRADE COUNT COLLAPSES FAR BELOW 223 -> the wider 40-bar high is now less often "above close" at
//        the moment of entry (rrOk binds harder), which would mean the fix traded selectivity for
//        distance rather than adding distance for free -- worth naming explicitly, not just noting.
//   REPORT avg loser, win rate and max drawdown together on every run (the board's standing
//   instruction after Attack 37 named the three drawdown categories).
strategy("BTC Attack52 RSI divergence scaled target", overlay=true,
     pyramiding=1, process_orders_on_close=true,
     commission_type=strategy.commission.percent, commission_value=0.05,
     initial_capital=10000,
     default_qty_type=strategy.percent_of_equity, default_qty_value=100,
     margin_long=100, margin_short=100)

leftBars  = input.int(5,   "Pivot left bars")
rightBars = input.int(5,   "Pivot right bars -- confirmation lag")
rsiLen    = input.int(14,  "RSI length")
tgtLook   = input.int(40,  "Target lookback -- prior N-bar high (2x Attack 51's 20)")
minRpct   = input.float(0.80, "Min stop distance as % of price (LESSON 3)")
maxBars   = input.int(192, "Max bars in trade")

rsiVal = ta.rsi(close, rsiLen)
pl     = ta.pivotlow(low, leftBars, rightBars)

var float lastPivLow = na
var float lastPivRSI = na
var float prevPivLow = na
var float prevPivRSI = na
var bool  divNow      = false

divNow := false
if not na(pl)
    prevPivLow := lastPivLow
    prevPivRSI := lastPivRSI
    lastPivLow := pl
    lastPivRSI := rsiVal[rightBars]
    if not na(prevPivLow) and lastPivLow < prevPivLow and lastPivRSI > prevPivRSI
        divNow := true

res = ta.highest(high, tgtLook)[1]

rLong = close - lastPivLow
minR  = close * minRpct / 100
rBig  = not na(lastPivLow) and rLong >= minR
rrOk  = not na(res) and res > close

goLong = divNow and rBig and rrOk

var float slPx   = na
var float tpPx   = na
var int   barsIn = 0

flat = strategy.position_size == 0

if flat and goLong
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
    slPx   := lastPivLow
    tpPx   := res
    barsIn := 0

if strategy.position_size > 0
    strategy.exit("LX", from_entry="L", stop=slPx, limit=tpPx)
    barsIn := barsIn + 1

if barsIn >= maxBars and strategy.position_size != 0
    strategy.close_all()
    barsIn := 0

plot(goLong ? 1 : 0, title="LongSignal")
plot(lastPivLow, title="LastPivotLow")
plot(res, title="TargetLevel")
